'\" t
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.\" Manual page for libaccudisc, the AccuDisc public C API.
.\" Requires the tbl(1) preprocessor (see the '\" t line above).
.TH ACCUDISC 8 "2026-07-29" "AccuDisc 0.4.0" "AccuDisc Library Reference"
.SH NAME
libaccudisc, accudisc \- AccuDisc CD\-DA capture and recording library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <accudisc/accudisc.h>
.B #include <accudisc/driver.h>
.PP
.B cc \fIfile.c\fB $(pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs accudisc)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libaccudisc
is a C shared library for low-level Red Book CD\-DA capture and Disc\-At\-Once
recording. It is the engine behind
.BR accudisc (1),
and the interface a front-end application is expected to use directly.
.PP
The public header
.I include/accudisc/accudisc.h
is the
.B contract.
Nothing under
.I src/
is part of the interface, and bindings are written against the header
exclusively. Every identifier is prefixed
.B accudisc_
or
.BR ACCUDISC_ ,
device handles are opaque, and no libc types leak into the ABI where that is
avoidable.
.PP
The library only moves bits. It performs no post-processing, no metadata
lookups, no encoding and no analysis; those belong to the calling application,
as do the absolute verification gates (AccurateRip, CTDB).
.SH VERSIONING
.nf
.B #define ACCUDISC_VERSION_MAJOR 0
.B #define ACCUDISC_VERSION_MINOR 3
.B #define ACCUDISC_VERSION_PATCH 0
.PP
.B const char *accudisc_version_string(void);
.B void accudisc_version(int *major, int *minor, int *patch);
.fi
.PP
The macros describe the header a caller compiled against; the functions report
the library actually linked. Comparing them detects header/library skew. The
current version is 0.4.0 and the soname remains
.IR libaccudisc.so.0 .
.SH ERROR MODEL
Every fallible function returns
.B ACCUDISC_OK
(0) or a negative
.BR accudisc_err .
.BR accudisc_strerror (3)-style
naming is provided by
.B accudisc_strerror(int)
which returns a static string.
.TS
lb lb lb
l l l.
value	name	meaning
0	ACCUDISC_OK	success
\-1	ACCUDISC_ERR_INVAL	invalid argument
\-2	ACCUDISC_ERR_NOMEM	allocation failure
\-3	ACCUDISC_ERR_OPEN	device would not open
\-4	ACCUDISC_ERR_IO	transport/driver failure
\-5	ACCUDISC_ERR_SENSE	drive: CHECK CONDITION
\-6	ACCUDISC_ERR_SHORT	response too short
\-7	ACCUDISC_ERR_UNSUPPORTED	drive or build lacks it
\-8	ACCUDISC_ERR_CANCELLED	cancelled by flag or sink
\-9	ACCUDISC_ERR_CRC	checksum failed
\-10	ACCUDISC_ERR_NOTFOUND	data legitimately absent
\-11	ACCUDISC_ERR_UNSAFE_COMBINATION	self-defeating request
\-12	ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI	bad struct \fBsize\fR
.TE
.PP
Three of these carry meaning a caller must not flatten.
.TP
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_NOTFOUND
The drive answered and the data legitimately is not there \(em no CD\-Text on
this disc, no ISRC on this track, no ATIP, no driver file. A drive that
.I rejects
the command returns
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_SENSE
instead. Conflating them turns
.RI \(lq "this disc has no CD\-Text" \(rq
into
.RI \(lq "this drive cannot read CD\-Text" \(rq,
and a binding that maps every non-OK value onto one exception loses exactly
that distinction.
.TP
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_UNSAFE_COMBINATION
The request would return silently corrupt data given the drive's current
state. It is never returned for a merely unusual request \(em only where the
corruption is known and measured. Today the one case is capturing subchannel
while the vendor read-speed uncap is authoritatively on. Where the request
struct offers an override field, the caller may proceed deliberately.
.TP
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI
A caller-allocated struct declared a
.B size
this build cannot honour. It means
.RI \(lq "rebuild against this header" \(rq,
not
.RI \(lq "fix your arguments" \(rq,
which is why it is distinct from
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_INVAL .
See
.B ABI SIZE NEGOTIATION
below.
.PP
.B ACCUDISC_WROTE_WITH_CAVEATS
(the value 1) is a
.B positive
return from
.BR accudisc_write ,
not an error: the burn
.I completed
but a caveat was logged. Test with
.RB \(lq "rc > 0" \(rq,
never
.RB \(lq "rc != ACCUDISC_OK" \(rq.
A caller testing
.RB \(lq "if (rc)" \(rq
treats a successful burn as a failure; one testing
.RB \(lq "if (rc < 0)" \(rq
silently drops the caveat. Both compile and neither is caught by a type check.
.PP
After a failure,
.B accudisc_last_sense()
returns the decoded SCSI sense (key, ASC, ASCQ, plus a
.I valid
flag), and
.B accudisc_last_io()
returns a short human string explaining the most recent
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_IO
\(em an I/O failure carries no sense data, so without it a transport failure
cannot be attributed after the fact. The string is owned by the device and is
valid only until the next command.
.SH OBJECT MODEL
.SS Device handles
.nf
.B typedef struct accudisc_device accudisc_device;
.PP
.B #define ACCUDISC_OPEN_RDWR 0x1u
.PP
.B accudisc_device *accudisc_open(const char *path, unsigned flags, int *err);
.B void accudisc_close(accudisc_device *dev);
.fi
.PP
.B accudisc_open()
returns NULL on failure and, when
.I err
is non-NULL, stores the
.B accudisc_err
cause there.
.B ACCUDISC_OPEN_RDWR
is required for vendor opcodes, MODE SELECT and writing, because the kernel's
unprivileged SG_IO command filter blocks those on a read-only descriptor. Plain
reading should not set it \(em least privilege.
.PP
.B accudisc_set_log(dev, fn, user)
installs an optional sink for library and driver diagnostics. The default is to
discard them. It is the only channel on which some information (for example the
specific write caveat) is reported at all.
.SS Buffer ownership
Buffers the library allocates for the caller \(em the raw TOC, full TOC and
CD\-Text blobs, and the decoded
.B accudisc_cdtext
\(em must be released with
.BR accudisc_free() ,
not with the caller's runtime free. Everything else is caller-allocated.
.SH ABI SIZE NEGOTIATION
.B accudisc_read_req
and
.B accudisc_read_stats
are caller-allocated, transparent, cross FFI boundaries, and have both grown in
place across this project's history (the request 32 \(-> 40 \(-> 56 bytes, the
stats 80 \(-> 104 \(-> 128). The CLI never noticed, because it is rebuilt with
the library. A binding compiled against one header and loaded against a
different shared object would have run off the end of a struct \(em in the worst
case reading garbage into a safety flag, producing well-formed data with the
wrong referent and nothing downstream able to tell.
.PP
So each carries its own size as its first field, and the caller sets it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.B accudisc_read_req   req = ACCUDISC_READ_REQ_INIT;
.B accudisc_read_stats st  = ACCUDISC_READ_STATS_INIT;
.fi
.RE
.PP
The two initialiser macros expand to a designated initialiser setting
.B .size
to
.BR sizeof() .
The rules are asymmetric because the direction of the write is:
.TP
.B IN (accudisc_read_req \(em the library reads it)
A
.B smaller
size than this build's is accepted and the missing tail is treated as zero, so
an older caller gets older behaviour. A
.B larger
size is accepted only if every byte past this build's end is zero; a nonzero
one means the caller is asking for a feature this library does not have, and
gets
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI
rather than silence.
.TP
.B OUT (accudisc_read_stats \(em the library writes it)
A
.B smaller
size is honoured by writing only that many bytes. A
.B larger
size is
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI :
the library would otherwise leave counters the caller believes in unfilled, and
a zero meaning
.RI \(lq "not computed" \(rq
is indistinguishable from a zero meaning
.RI \(lq "none observed" \(rq.
.PP
A
.B zero
size is always
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI .
It is what a caller that forgot the macro produces, so forgetting fails loudly
on the first call instead of scribbling. The only values with a meaning are
.B sizeof()
as some released header saw it.
.PP
Structs that do
.I not
carry a size are frozen: growing one is a soname bump, and the test suite pins
their sizes so that growth cannot happen by accident.
.B accudisc_chunk
is the one that matters, because there the hazard runs the other way \(em the
library allocates it and the sink reads it. It has been 32 bytes since it was
introduced.
.SH READING
.nf
.B int accudisc_read_cdda(accudisc_device *dev,
.B "                       const accudisc_read_req *req,"
.B "                       accudisc_sink_fn sink, void *user,"
.B "                       accudisc_read_stats *stats);"
.fi
.PP
Blocking. Streams
.I req\->count
sectors starting at
.I req\->lba
to
.IR sink ,
which may be NULL to read for status and statistics only.
.I stats
may be NULL.
.PP
The caller says
.I what
(the range),
.I with what companions
(C2 via
.BR ACCUDISC_C2_NONE / _PTRS / _PTRS_BEB ,
subchannel via
.BR ACCUDISC_SUB_NONE / _RAW / _Q )
and
.I how
(chunking, retries, speed, and the accuracy strategy:
.IR c2_retries ,
.IR verify_passes ,
.IR overlap_sectors ,
.IR speed_ladder ).
With every accuracy field zero the read is a single-pass fast capture.
.PP
Audio, C2 and subchannel for a given sector always come from the
.B same READ CD transfer.
That single-read alignment is the property C2-guided recovery depends on, and
it is why a rescued sector is replaced whole rather than field by field.
.PP
.I req\->status_map,
when non-NULL, must point at
.I count
bytes and receives one status byte per sector, updated in place as the read
proceeds. The encoding is
.BR ACCUDISC_MAP_STATE() " / " ACCUDISC_MAP_SEVERITY()
over the
.B ACCUDISC_MAP_*
constants; see
.BR accudisc (1)
for the table. Reading the map from another thread while the device is being
driven is safe and is the intended progress-tracking pattern.
.PP
.I req\->subq_map
is a second, independent lane with the same size, lifetime and live-read
semantics, holding the Q-subchannel health of each delivered sector:
.BR ACCUDISC_SUBQ_STATE() " over the " ACCUDISC_SUBQ_*
constants, severity always 0. It
.B requires
.IR req\->sub " == " ACCUDISC_SUB_RAW
and returns
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_INVAL
otherwise. Neither map is derivable from the other \(em audio and Q fail
independently \(em and in particular an unreadable sector is
.B ACCUDISC_SUBQ_NO_AUDIO
here rather than a CRC failure, because the zero-filled frame such a sector
delivers does fail CRC-16 and would otherwise be recorded as damage that is not
on the disc. See
.BR accudisc (1).
.PP
.I req\->cancel,
when non-NULL, is polled between chunks; a nonzero value aborts the read with
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_CANCELLED .
.SS The sink callback
.nf
.B typedef struct accudisc_chunk {
.B "    uint32_t lba;"
.B "    uint32_t nsec;"
.B "    const uint8_t *data;"
.B "    uint32_t sector_len;"
.B "    uint32_t audio_len;"
.B "    uint32_t c2_len;"
.B "    uint32_t sub_len;"
.B "} accudisc_chunk;"
.PP
.B typedef int (*accudisc_sink_fn)(void *user, const accudisc_chunk *chunk);
.fi
.PP
.I data
holds
.I nsec
consecutive sectors of
.I sector_len
bytes each, laid out AUDIO
.RI ( audio_len )
then C2
.RI ( c2_len )
then SUB
.RI ( sub_len ).
Hard-unreadable sectors arrive zero-filled with an all-ones C2 bitmap, so the
streams never desync and the delivered sector count always equals the requested
one.
.PP
.B The buffer is library-owned and valid only for the duration of the call.
A pointer retained past the callback's return reads freed memory. Copy what you
need, or consume it in place.
.PP
Returning 0 continues the read; any nonzero value cancels it and
.B accudisc_read_cdda()
returns
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_CANCELLED .
.SS Statistics
.B accudisc_read_stats
reports totals over the completed read: sectors read, C2-flagged sectors and
total fired C2 bits, hard errors broken down by sense key, the first and last
flagged LBA (\-1 when none), the consensus outcomes
.RI ( sectors_recovered ,
.IR sectors_suspect ,
.IR rereads ),
.I slips
(disagreements that were a pure positional shift \(em the C2-invisible slip
class; a nonzero count says use overlap checking on this drive), and the
Q-subchannel CRC census
.RI ( subq_total ,
.IR subq_ok ),
counted only for raw-subchannel reads. The subchannel has no CIRC protection;
its per-frame CRC\-16 is its only integrity check and it fails independently of
the audio C2 figures.
.SH DEVICE AND DISC INTERROGATION
Selected calls; the header is the full list and carries the per-call semantics.
.TP
.B accudisc_drive_identify()
INQUIRY vendor/product/revision, space-trimmed.
.TP
.B accudisc_read_offset()
The drive's manufacturing read offset in samples from the built-in table;
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_NOTFOUND
when the model is unknown.
.TP
.BR accudisc_read_toc() ", " accudisc_read_toc_src()
READ TOC format 0, parsed. The
.I _src
form additionally reports which physical operation answered and, on a fallback,
why \(em format 2 (the lead-in, carrying session structure) and format 0 (the
drive's decoded descriptors) are different operations, not two views of one
thing, and a marginal lead-in can fail one while the other answers perfectly.
.TP
.BR accudisc_read_full_toc() ", " accudisc_fulltoc_parse()
The raw format-2 blob and its parser.
.TP
.BR accudisc_read_cdtext() ", " accudisc_cdtext_decode()
The raw format-5 pack blob and its decoder. Decoding covers block 0, the first
language, single-byte character packs, and the title / performer / songwriter /
UPC\-ISRC types. Bytes are copied through verbatim with no character-set
conversion, so UTF\-8-authored discs pass through undamaged and the caller
interprets.
.TP
.B accudisc_probe_disc()
The pre-flight disc-kind guard behind
.BR "accudisc disc" .
Composes GET CONFIGURATION, READ DISC INFORMATION and the track census; the
profile gate precedes the census deliberately, so a non-CD medium cannot be
promoted by its track counts.
.TP
.BR accudisc_probe_features() ", " accudisc_probe_accurate_stream() ", " accudisc_probe_c2_lag() ", " accudisc_probe_speed_ladder()
Capability and behaviour probes. The speed-ladder probe is the only ground
truth for what a rung actually delivers: mode page 2A reports the
.IR setting ,
not reality.
.TP
.BR accudisc_read_atip() ", " accudisc_atip_manufacturer()
Recordable-media identification. All fields are reported raw as the disc
encodes them.
.TP
.BR accudisc_scan_mcn() ", " accudisc_scan_isrc() ", " accudisc_scan_pregaps()
Q-subchannel metadata. The pregap scan's window and its one-read-per-boundary
rule live in the library so that every binding scans identically.
.TP
.BR accudisc_check_audio_range() ", " accudisc_plan_read_range()
The range guard and the request planner. Both are pure functions over a TOC, so
a caller can vet a range without touching the drive. Every refusal returns the
same error code and the detail is in the reason field \(em message selection
belongs to the front end, not the library.
.SH WRITING
.nf
.B int accudisc_write(accudisc_device *dev, const char *toc_path,
.B "                   const char *bin_path,"
.B "                   const accudisc_write_opts *opts,"
.B "                   void (*progress)(void *user, uint32_t done,"
.B "                                    uint32_t total),"
.B "                   void *user);"
.fi
.PP
Burns one audio session Disc\-At\-Once from a cdrdao
.I .toc
and the raw s16 audio image it names. Requires a blank disc and an
.B ACCUDISC_OPEN_RDWR
handle.
.B accudisc_write_opts
carries
.IR simulate ,
.I byteswap
and
.IR speed ,
plus
.I cdtext_path
\(em a raw READ TOC format-0x05 blob laid into the lead-in verbatim, byte-for-byte
as
.B accudisc_read_cdtext()
emits it.
.PP
The struct leads with
.I size
and the caller must set it, which
.B ACCUDISC_WRITE_OPTS_INIT
does:
.PP
.nf
.B "    accudisc_write_opts o = ACCUDISC_WRITE_OPTS_INIT;"
.fi
.PP
The rules are the IN half of the negotiation described for
.B accudisc_read_req
above \(em a shorter struct is zero-extended, a longer one is accepted only if
every byte past this build's end is zero, and a declared size of 0 is
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI .
The guard matters more here than on the read path: this is the only entry point
in the library that is not idempotent, so a field read past the end of a short
caller's struct does not return a wrong answer to be checked later, it burns a
disc.
.PP
Return values:
.B ACCUDISC_OK
for a clean burn or clean simulate;
.B ACCUDISC_WROTE_WITH_CAVEATS
when the burn completed but see the log;
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
when the disc is not blank, in which case
.I nothing
was written;
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI
when
.I opts\->size
is 0 or declares fields this build cannot honour, in which case nothing was
written and nothing was read past the struct; any other negative
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_*
for a transport, parse or local error. A negative return means the burn did not
complete; a non-negative return means it did.
.PP
This API is marked provisional in the header: the write engine is young and its
options struct may grow \(em which is why it carries
.IR size .
.SH VENDOR DRIVERS
.B libaccudisc
itself is pure MMC/SG. No proprietary opcode is ever compiled into the core.
Hardware-specific features live in external shared objects named
.IR accudisc\-drv\- NAME .so ,
loaded at runtime only when the calling application permits it \(em
.B calling
.B accudisc_driver_attach() IS the permission grant.
Without it a device never issues a vendor opcode.
.PP
.nf
.B int accudisc_driver_attach(accudisc_device *dev, const char *name,
.B "                           const char *dir);"
.B void accudisc_driver_detach(accudisc_device *dev);
.B const char *accudisc_access_method(accudisc_device *dev);
.fi
.PP
.I name
requests a specific driver, or NULL auto-matches the identified drive.
.I dir
overrides the search directory, or NULL uses
.B $ACCUDISC_DRIVER_DIR
falling back to the installed default. The attach order is enforced by the
library:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 4
the drive is identified (INQUIRY);
.IP 2. 4
a driver is located, by explicit name or by matching the drive ID;
.IP 3. 4
the calling application's permission is implied by the attach call itself;
.IP 4. 4
.B selftest()
must demonstrate that the opcode path genuinely works on this drive, by
reading, setting and re-reading real device state;
.IP 5. 4
on any failure the device silently remains generic MMC/SG, fully usable.
.RE
.PP
.B accudisc_driver_attach()
returns
.B ACCUDISC_OK
when attached,
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_NOTFOUND
when no driver file matched (a warn-only situation), or
.B ACCUDISC_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
when a driver was found but its selftest failed.
.B accudisc_access_method()
returns a never-NULL human string \(em
.RI \(lq "generic MMC" \(rq
or
.RI \(lq "driver <name> (<description>)" \(rq
\(em so an application can log which path it is on. Vendor opcodes need the
kernel's full SG_IO command set, so the device must be opened with
.B ACCUDISC_OPEN_RDWR
or the selftest will fail.
.SS Driver capabilities exposed today
.TP
.B Hardware error counters
.BR accudisc_counter_scan_begin() ,
.BR accudisc_counter_scan_read() ,
.BR accudisc_counter_scan_end() ,
and the composed
.B accudisc_counter_census()
which arms, scans a span sampling every
.B ACCUDISC_CENSUS_CADENCE
(75) sectors, and disarms on every exit path \(em which is the reason it exists
as one call rather than three. 75 sectors is one second of audio, and that is
why the reported figures are comparable with other C1/C2 tools.
.TP
.B Read-speed uncap
.BR accudisc_speed_uncap_get() " / " accudisc_speed_uncap_set()
toggle it;
.B accudisc_speed_uncap_probe()
reports it as
.BR ACCUDISC_UNCAP_OFF ", " ACCUDISC_UNCAP_ON
(both authoritative),
.B ACCUDISC_UNCAP_LIKELY_ON
(inferred from the drive's reported maximum exceeding this model's known stock
ceiling) or
.B ACCUDISC_UNCAP_UNKNOWN
(no driver, and the model's stock ceiling has not been verified \(em which is
not
.RI \(lq off \(rq).
The library refuses a read only on the authoritative values, because refusing
on a guess would leave a caller unable to capture subchannel at all on a drive
we merely fail to recognise.
.IP
The setting is
.B persistent drive state:
it survives the handle and the process.
.BR accudisc_speed_uncap_push() " / " accudisc_speed_uncap_pop()
are the scoped form \(em push reads the prior value first and does not attempt
the set if that read fails, and stores \-1 in
.I *prior_out
when there is nothing to restore, so pop can be called unconditionally on every
exit path including error paths.
.SS Writing a driver
.I include/accudisc/driver.h
is the SDK. A driver never links against
.BR libaccudisc :
it receives an
.B accudisc_host
(callbacks for raw command execution and logging) and returns a static
.B accudisc_driver
descriptor from its single exported entry point,
.PP
.RS 4
.B const accudisc_driver *accudisc_driver_entry(void);
.RE
.PP
The descriptor's
.IR abi ", " name ", " match " and " selftest
are mandatory;
.I abi
must equal
.B ACCUDISC_DRIVER_ABI
(currently 2) or the library refuses the module. Capability slots may be NULL,
meaning not offered.
.PP
The bundled
.B plextor
driver implements exactly two capabilities \(em the C1/C2/CU error-counter scan
and the read-speed uncap. Other Plextor features have been reverse-engineered
and pinned but are
.B not
reachable through this API; see
.I drivers/plextor/FEATURES.md
for the distinction between an opcode exchange verified on hardware and a
feature wired into the driver.
.SH THREADING AND DEVICE SHARING
Device handles are
.B not thread-safe.
Use one handle per thread, or serialise access externally. Reading a status map
while another thread drives the same device is safe, and is the intended
progress-tracking pattern.
.PP
Beyond a single process, an optical drive is a single shared resource with
.B persistent state:
the read-speed setting, the vendor uncap, and the drive's own error counters
all outlive a handle. Two processes driving one drive concurrently will
interfere in ways that look like a bad disc rather than like contention. Take an
external lock around the device node.
.PP
Setting a read-speed ceiling through SET STREAMING requires
.BR CAP_SYS_RAWIO ;
without it the library falls back to the unprivileged CDROM_SELECT_SPEED path,
which drives treat as advisory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open a device, identify it, and report the access method:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.B #include <accudisc/accudisc.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B "int err = 0;"
.B "accudisc_device *dev = accudisc_open(\(dq/dev/sr0\(dq, 0, &err);"
.PP
.B "if (!dev) {"
.B "        fprintf(stderr, \(dqopen: %s\en\(dq, accudisc_strerror(err));"
.B "        return 2;"
.B "}"
.PP
.B "accudisc_drive_id id;"
.PP
.B "if (accudisc_drive_identify(dev, &id) == ACCUDISC_OK)"
.B "        printf(\(dq%s %s %s via %s\en\(dq, id.vendor, id.product,"
.B "               id.revision, accudisc_access_method(dev));"
.B "accudisc_close(dev);"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the TOC and print the audio tracks:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.B "accudisc_toc toc;"
.PP
.B "if (accudisc_read_toc(dev, &toc) == ACCUDISC_OK)"
.B "        for (uint8_t i = 0; i < toc.track_count; i++) {"
.B "                const accudisc_track *t = &toc.tracks[i];"
.PP
.B "                if (!ACCUDISC_TRACK_IS_AUDIO(t))"
.B "                        continue;"
.B "                printf(\(dqtrack %u lba %u\en\(dq, t->number, t->lba);"
.B "        }"
.fi
.RE
.PP
A capture with a sink callback and a status map. Note the size macros, and that
the chunk buffer is only valid inside the callback:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.B "static int sink(void *user, const accudisc_chunk *c)"
.B "{"
.B "        FILE *pcm = user;"
.PP
.B "        for (uint32_t s = 0; s < c->nsec; s++)"
.B "                fwrite(c->data + (size_t)s * c->sector_len, 1,"
.B "                       c->audio_len, pcm);"
.B "        return 0;   /* nonzero cancels the read */"
.B "}"
.PP
.B "accudisc_read_req   req = ACCUDISC_READ_REQ_INIT;"
.B "accudisc_read_stats st  = ACCUDISC_READ_STATS_INIT;"
.B "uint8_t *map = calloc(count, 1);"
.PP
.B "req.lba = start;"
.B "req.count = count;"
.B "req.c2 = ACCUDISC_C2_PTRS;"
.B "req.sub = ACCUDISC_SUB_RAW;"
.B "req.c2_retries = 8;"
.B "req.verify_passes = 2;"
.B "req.status_map = map;"
.PP
.B "int rc = accudisc_read_cdda(dev, &req, sink, pcm, &st);"
.PP
.B "if (rc == ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI)"
.B "        fprintf(stderr, \(dqrebuild against this accudisc.h\en\(dq);"
.B "else if (rc == ACCUDISC_OK && (st.hard_errors || st.sectors_suspect))"
.B "        fprintf(stderr, \(dqdelivered, but degraded\en\(dq);"
.fi
.RE
.SH LANGUAGE BINDINGS
Python and Rust bindings are
.B work in progress.
.I bindings/python/
and
.I bindings/rust/
exist as placeholders; nothing is implemented yet. The design is settled: a
streaming API layered over the sink callback, generated against this header
\(em never a subprocess wrapper around
.BR accudisc (1),
and never written against
.IR src/ .
.PP
A binding reproduces the
.I semantics
of the CLI's process conventions (exit codes,
.BR \-\-progress\-fd ,
terminal rendering), not their mechanism. The mapping from each exit code to
the library values that encode the same decision is tabulated in
.IR docs/reference/cli\-machine\-interface.md .
.PP
Two binding-specific hazards are worth repeating: buffers the library allocated
must be released through
.BR accudisc_free() ,
not the runtime's own allocator; and every
.B accudisc_read_req
/
.B accudisc_read_stats
must have its
.B size
field set, or the first call fails with
.BR ACCUDISC_ERR_ABI .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACCUDISC_DRIVER_DIR
Directory searched for vendor driver modules when
.B accudisc_driver_attach()
is passed a NULL
.IR dir .
If unset, the installed driver directory compiled into the library is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I include/accudisc/accudisc.h
The public API contract.
.TP
.I include/accudisc/driver.h
The vendor-driver SDK.
.TP
.IR <libdir> /accudisc/drivers/
Installed vendor driver modules.
.SH CREDITS
The library's code is original, but knowledge in it was learned from prior art:
the drive read-offset table is factual data from the
.B REDUMP Disc Preservation Project
(<https://redump.org>); command layouts and drive quirks were documented by
.BR redumper ", " cdrtools ", " cdrdao " and " libcdio\-paranoia ;
and the Plextor vendor command set used by the bundled driver is documented in
.B QPxTool
(GPL-2.0), credited as a courtesy reference \(em no source is copied, and every
command was independently verified on hardware. The full record, which this
summarises, is
.IR docs/reference/ATTRIBUTION.md .
See
.BR accudisc (1)
for the expanded version.
